A 43-year-old man presents to your clinic
concerned about his risk of developing prostate
cancer. The concern arose when his father was
diagnosed with prostate cancer at the age of 88
years a few months ago. His worry was worse
when he realized that his neighbour has prostate
cancer as well. The neighbor has told him that
there is screening test for early detection of
prostate cancer. He asks to undergo screening
after you fully explained to him the pros and cons
of screening protocols and the uncertainty. On
digital rectal exam (DRE), prostate is smooth and
of normal size and shape. The medial sulcus is felt.
Which one of the following is the next best step in
management?','{"A":"Reassure him.","B":"Order a transrectal ultrasonography.","C":"Annual DRE.","D":"Perform prostate-specific antigen (PSA)\n\ntesting in two weeks.","E":"Biannual DRE.\n\n0"}','D',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-53fcec143cd2","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"aa8e1a0b70ceda5498dc","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":62,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"aa8e1a0b70ceda5498dc","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":62,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"oat > 76\nA 43-year-old man presents to your clinic\nconcerned about his risk of developing prostate\ncancer. The concern arose when his father was\ndiagnosed with prostate cancer at the age of 88\nyears a few months ago. His worry was worse\nwhen he realized that his neighbour has prostate\ncancer as well. The neighbor has told him that\nthere is screening test for early detection of\nprostate cancer. He asks to undergo screening\nafter you fully explained to him the pros and cons\nof screening protocols and the uncertainty. On\ndigital rectal exam (DRE), prostate is smooth and\nof normal size and shape. The medial sulcus is felt.\nWhich one of the following is the next best step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Reassure him.","B":"Order a transrectal ultrasonography.","C":"Annual DRE.","D":"Perform prostate-specific antigen (PSA)\n\ntesting in two weeks.","E":"Biannual DRE.\n\n0"},"source_answer":"D",