aortic aneurysm. The aneurysm was repaired by a
vascular surgeon, and the patient was transferred
to the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) where he
stayed for 24 hours. The recovery period was
uneventful. The patient is now ready to be
discharged, and wants to know whether he can
drive his private car. Which one of the following is
the most appropriate advice regarding driving?','{"A":"He is unfit to drive for six months post-\nrepair.","B":"He is unfit to drive for six months as he\n\nhas been in intensive care unit.","C":"He can drive after he spends a week at\nhome without any symptoms.","D":"After his general practitioner considers\nhim fit to drive.","E":"He is unfit to drive for four weeks."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-155b4f66bede","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"22c6a592aab2732db2e4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":93,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"c29dc4000814f7b9d35d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":92,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"1b80b4dc64077e22d637","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1670,"source_qid":"721"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"22c6a592aab2732db2e4","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":93,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 65-year-old was found to have an abdominal\naortic aneurysm. The aneurysm was repaired by a\nvascular surgeon, and the patient was transferred\nto the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) where he\nstayed for 24 hours. The recovery period was\nuneventful. The patient is now ready to be\ndischarged, and wants to know whether he can\