in sustains a needle stick injury while she is setting
up a new intravenous line for a patient. The
patient is HBsAg negative. History reveals that the
patient is unlikely to be within the window period.
The nurse is unsure of her hepatitis B
immunization status. Which one of the following is
the most appropriate next step in management?','{"A":"No further follow up is required.","B":"Give hepatitis B immunoglobulin and full\ncourse of hepatitis B vaccination.","C":"Organize a full course of hepatitis B\nimmunization.","D":"Report the incidence to the infectious\ndisease specialist.","E":"Perform a blood test to check the HBsAg\nstatus in 3 months.\n\nEn ES Oo"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ae8078e53b03","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f2506f8864ba9efc7e2e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":212,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"09a45c40a20742366559","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":211,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"f18768657e7725833df8","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1699,"source_qid":"991"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"f2506f8864ba9efc7e2e","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":212,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"One of the nurses of the ward you are working\nin sustains a needle stick injury while she is setting\nup a new intravenous line for a patient. The\npatient is HBsAg negative. History reveals that the\npatient is unlikely to be within the window period.\nThe nurse is unsure of her hepatitis B\nimmunization status. W