practice for vaccination. Three weeks ago, the boy
had a fever and rash suggestive of rubella
infection. Which one of the following will be the
most appropriate step in management?','{"A":"Vaccinate him with MMR vaccine now.","B":"Order a serum anti-rubella antibody to\nguide further decision.","C":"Do not give rubella vaccine as he is\nalready immune.","D":"Tell her she should wait until the boy\nturns 12 months before MMR\nvaccination.","E":"Vaccinate him at 15 months of age."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0c37e8672ed7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7dfbe8ccedaca4ca4563","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":218,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"6fa602d29c824a3702b4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (2).pdf","source_page":32,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"e7715c73546909587e1c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":217,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"69833a11c60fc8fa5b2d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1700,"source_qid":"1021"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"7dfbe8ccedaca4ca4563","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":218,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Mother of an 11-month-old boy brings him to your\npractice for vaccination. Three weeks ago, the boy\nhad a fever and rash sug