A 25-year-old woman presents with a history of
greenish-yellow vaginal discharge. Testing for
sexually transmissible infections (STIs) is positive for
chlamydia infection. The woman has had multiple sex
partners in the past six months. Which one of the
following would be the most appropriate advice for
her in terms of priority?','{"A":"CYA Trace all her sexual contacts in the past\nsix months and treat them.","B":"Ask her to bring her most recent sexual\ncontacts for testing and treatment.","C":"Ask her to practice safe sex.","D":"CD Advise that she should not use intrauterine\ncontraception devices until there is no\ninfection.","E":"CE Tell that she should report her infection to\nthe relevant health authorities."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-5728fab6b9f8","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b0addc4b6e033b605f6c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_page":361,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.8.2-residual-resolver-page-checkpoint-local-render-2026-09-23","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"b0addc4b6e033b605f6c","source_file":"Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex PB 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":361,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"> 19:51 atl > 345-—-\nA 25-year-old woman presents with a history of\ngreenish-yellow vaginal discharge. Testing for\nsexually transmissible infections (STIs) is positive for\nchlamydia infection. The woman has had multiple sex\npartners in the past six months. Which one of the\nfollowing would be the most appropriate advice for\nher in terms of priority?","options":{"A":"CYA Trace all her sexual contacts in the past\nsix months and treat them.","B":"Ask her to bring her most recent sexual\ncontacts for testing and treatment.","C":"Ask her to practice safe sex.","D":"CD Advise that she should not use intrauterine\ncontraception devices until there is no\ninfec